 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 515426,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "When you flip a coin, there are 2 possible outcomes: heads and tails. Let’s say you flip a coin 10 times, and after each you write down the result of the flip (H for heads, T for tails). How many different results (strings of 10 characters, where each is either an H or a T) are possible?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The Multiplication Rule of Counting says that if there are <i>n</i> ways to accomplish one task and <i>m</i> ways to accomplish a second task, then there are <span data-math=\"n{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}m\"></span> ways to accomplish both tasks. You can tack on additional tasks by multiplying the number of ways to accomplish those tasks to your previous product.</p>\n<p>Each time you flip, you have two choices.</p>\n<p>You flip ten times, so you have two choices each flip.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}2{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} \\times 2{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}1,024\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "1,024"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
